    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48524" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεσμο-φύλαξ</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ακος</span>, ὁ</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>guardian of the law</i>,
			of <i><span class="en">
				Moses
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.171
			</span></i>:—usu. in pl. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεσμο-φύλακες</span></b> , οἱ, a
			magistracy at Elis, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.47
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				5.67
			</span></i>; at Alexandria, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PHal.</u>
				1.239
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>; in Ceos, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(5).595
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>B</u>
				16
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii/ii B.C.)</span>; at Ptolemais, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PFay.</u>
				22.11
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A.D.)</span>; 
				Boeot.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεθμοφούλαξ</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				7.3172.178
			</span></i> (Orchom.): —hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεσμο-φῠλάκιον</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], τό</span>, their office, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PHal.</u>
				1.234
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>:</div>
